Single global DB interface (database.DB)

Allows you to switch database implementation in the future (MongoDB → MySQL/Postgres) without changing middleware.

Domain-based database selection (GetDatabase(domain))

Each request gets the correct DB based on the Domain header.

Caches domain -> *mongo.Database in domainDBMap to avoid repeated Database() calls.

Middleware injection (ValidateDomain)

Injects domain DB into Gin Context for each request.

Prevents code duplication — all handlers just read from c.Get("db").

LoadDomains preloading

Reduces the need to hit master DB every time, which is good for performance.

Separation of concerns

mongodb.go handles DB logic.

database.go contains the interface.

helper.ValidateDomain just checks DB existence.